        "original_id": "e6a457d4-0faa-5572-a968-e9d58f51bd50",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lithocarpus, Duranta\n- Taxonomy: Fagaceae, Quercus, genus, species\n- Concepts: flower morphology, native range\n\nFacts:\n- Lithocarpus is a genus in the beech family Fagaceae.\n- Lithocarpus differs from Quercus by having erect spikes of insect-pollinated male flowers.\n- Lithocarpus differs from Quercus by having female flowers with short styles and punctate stigmas.\n- Duranta contains 17 species of shrubs and small trees.\n- Duranta is native from southern Florida to Mexico and South America.",
